`mech build`
===============================================================================

`mech build` produces a release native executable by default. Use `--emit` to
request official bytecode v1, a native build plan, or a generated Cargo project.

1. Default native build
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sh
mech build main.mec \
  --out target/mech/main
```

`--out` is the exact artifact path. On Windows, the output may use the platform
executable suffix. The default build profile is `release`.

2. Bytecode
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sh
mech build main.mec \
  --emit bytecode \
  --out target/mech/main.mecb
```

This writes official bytecode v1 and does not invoke Cargo.

3. Build plan
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sh
mech build main.mec \
  --emit plan \
  --workspace-root . \
  --out target/mech/main.build-plan.json
```

4. Cargo project
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sh
mech build main.mec \
  --emit cargo-project \
  --workspace-root . \
  --out target/mech/main.cargo
```

The emitted Cargo project is directly buildable:

```sh
cargo build \
  --manifest-path target/mech/main.cargo/Cargo.toml \
  --locked
```

5. Direct bytecode input
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sh
mech build target/mech/main.mecb \
  --workspace-root . \
  --out target/mech/main-from-bytecode
```

6. Options
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```text
--emit native|bytecode|plan|cargo-project
--name
--out
--target
--profile debug|release
--config
--no-config
--workspace-root
--offline
--keep-project
```

Without `--workspace-root`, generated applications use exact registry component
dependencies. With `--workspace-root`, they use the selected packages from that
checkout.

`--keep-project` places a destination-adjusted generated Cargo project beside
the requested artifact.
